  "description": "A ring line (schema 27, ARCHITECTURE decision 49) on a loop of grid track: (1,1) to (5,1) along the top, (5,1) to (5,3) down the east, (5,3) to (1,3) along the bottom, (1,3) to (1,1) up the west. Alpha(3,0) has platform (3,1), Beta(6,2) (5,2), Gamma(3,4) (3,3), Delta(0,2) (1,2); from each to the next round the loop is three links, 3072 units. A ring needs three stops or more and not the same station first and last (Short A-B and Back A-B-A cannot be one), and no patterns; making Ring one makes its counts even, down (5, 2, 1 to 4, 2, 0), and from then on it refuses patterns and stop lists that are not a ring, and keeps odd counts even (3 to 2). Setting a line that is not a ring to a line changes nothing. Ring plans with a crawl { acceleration 125, braking 100, topSpeed 1 }: a leg accelerates for 8 s, runs at 1 km/h and brakes for 10 s, 181.8 s, so 182; the lap the inner way is four legs, the last Delta to Alpha, and a minute at each stop, no terminal: 968 s, 17 minutes; the journey starts at Alpha's platform facing north (every heading ties on the grid, the first wins). At most 17 / 2 = 8 trains each way, 16 in all; with one each way the headway is 17 and every segment carries 1440 / 17 rounded up = 85 a day; a target of 5 runs 17 / 5 rounded up = 4 each way, 8, at 5 (288 a day). Inner and Outer stand at Alpha, Inner facing east and Outer west; Inner (the lower ID) runs the inner way, Alpha-Beta-Gamma-Delta-Alpha, Outer the outer way, Alpha-Delta-Gamma-Beta-Alpha. At 00:00 each way sends its train out (lastDispatch and outerLastDispatch 0): it leaves Alpha after the least dwell, 36 s (no terminal on a ring), and each stop is 182 + 60 s after the one before, never reversing: 0/36, 218/278, 460/520, 702/762, 944/944. The lap ends at 980 s, so at 00:17, before that minute's dispatch, both stand at Alpha facing the way they came round.",
